<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Talos runs UNSANDBOXED. `com.apple.security.app-sandbox` is deliberately
  absent from this file, and adding it is a defect rather than a hardening
  improvement.

  The reason is a SPEC decision, stated on the wiki and not restated here:
  https://github.com/CalixtoTheBugHunter/talos/wiki/Technology-and-Distribution#decisions
  https://github.com/CalixtoTheBugHunter/talos/wiki/Technology-and-Distribution#why-unsandboxed-is-safe-here

  Binding line:
  > | Sandboxing | **Unsandboxed** — required for spawning agent CLIs and free
  > filesystem access |

  The burden of restraint therefore sits on Talos rather than on the OS, and it
  is met by the Safeguards layer:
  https://github.com/CalixtoTheBugHunter/talos/wiki/Safeguards-and-Autonomy
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
